│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ balance_then_local_search                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The original greedily assigns models in descending r/s order to the GPU with the          │
│                          │ currently lowest KVPR. I keep the feasibility handling but improve it with two ideas: (1) │
│                          │ assign each model to the GPU that minimizes the *resulting* KVPR after placement (a       │
│                          │ best-fit look-ahead), and (2) add a local-search refinement pass that repeatedly moves a  │
│                          │ model from the max-KVPR GPU to another GPU whenever it reduces the global maximum KVPR.   │
│                          │ This hill-climbing fix-up escapes the greedy's early bad commitments while staying simple │
│                          │ and fast.                                                                                 │
