│ patch_description        │ Improvement over the original: the original picks the GPU with the lowest KVPR *before*   │
│                          │ placing the model, which ignores how the placement changes the ratio. Instead, for each   │
│                          │ model we evaluate the KVPR of each candidate GPU *after* adding the model (sum(r/s)/(mem  │
│                          │ - sum(size))) and choose the GPU yielding the smallest resulting KVPR. Then a simple      │
│                          │ local-search pass repeatedly tries moving one model from the worst-KVPR GPU to another    │
│                          │ GPU if it lowers the global maximum KVPR. This keeps the code simple, fast, and correctly │
│                          │ memory-feasible, while lowering max KVPR.                                                 │
