                         Patch Metadata - Gen 8/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ post_placement_kvpr_and_local_search                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current greedy picks the GPU with the lowest *current* KVPR (weighted_req_rate /      │
│                          │ remaining memory), which ignores both the new model's contribution and the fact that      │
│                          │ denominator should be total used memory (GPU_MEM_SIZE - free), not remaining. This biases │
│                          │ placements badly. I fix the selection criterion to the *post-placement* KVPR: (load +     │
│                          │ r/s) / (GPU_MEM_SIZE - (free - size)), matching the evaluator's KVPR definition. Then I   │
│                          │ add a lightweight local-search pass that repeatedly moves a model off the hottest GPU     │
│                          │ (highest KVPR) whenever it strictly lowers the max KVPR across all GPUs, with bounded     │
│                          │ iterations. This directly minimizes the objective.                                        │
