│ patch_description        │ The current greedy only considers the GPU's existing load ratio, not the resulting KVPR   │
│                          │ after placing the model, and does no refinement. Replace with best-fit greedy (choose GPU │
│                          │ minimizing resulting KVPR) plus a local-search move phase that repeatedly tries to move   │
│                          │ models off the worst GPU whenever it lowers the global max KVPR. This mirrors the prior   │
│                          │ successful approach and should substantially reduce max KVPR while remaining simple and   │
│                          │ safe (with feasibility checks and reverts).                                               │
