│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kvpr_aware_greedy_plus_local_search                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current greedy assigns each model to the GPU with the lowest current load/free-mem    │
│                          │ ratio, but the correct objective is the resulting KVPR after placement: (load + w) /      │
│                          │ (GPU_MEM_SIZE - (free - size)). Selecting the GPU that directly minimizes the             │
│                          │ post-placement KVPR gives a strictly better greedy. On top of that, add a local-search    │
│                          │ pass that repeatedly moves a model off the GPU with maximum KVPR to another GPU whenever  │
│                          │ it reduces the global maximum KVPR. This mimics the well-known "minimize makespan via LPT │
│                          │ + local improvement" strategy: greedy seeding plus move-based refinement drives the       │
│                          │ maximum KVPR down toward the optimal balanced partition.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
