│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ seed_perturbation_restarts                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a randomized multi-restart wrapper around the greedy + local-search placement. For    │
│                          │ each restart, use a small random tie-break/tax on GPU selection (seeded via a provided    │
│                          │ rng) so different restarts explore different placements, then keep the best (lowest max   │
│                          │ KVPR) result. This diversifies beyond the deterministic greedy, which can get stuck in    │
│                          │ lockstep, while remaining simple and fast. The seeded random tax on the candidate GPU's   │
│                          │ KVPR perturbs tie-breaks among near-equal candidates. Only accept a restart's result if   │
│                          │ it improves the best max KVPR found so far. A fallback deterministic run is included so   │
│                          │ the algorithm always returns a valid placement.                                           │
