│ patch_name               │ add_two_for_one_swaps                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current local-search loop only tries 1-for-1 moves, and its measured score (0/1) is   │
│                          │ far worse than the plain greedy (21.89), suggesting the move-only refinement is both weak │
│                          │ and problematic. Following the recommendation, I extend the refinement phase to also      │
│                          │ perform swap moves: exchange one model on the worst GPU with one model from another GPU   │
│                          │ (1-for-1), and additionally try replacing one model on the worst GPU with two models from │
│                          │ GPU g (2-for-1), reusing the same feasibility pattern (recompute both GPUs' free memory,  │
│                          │ skip if any denominator drops to ≤0, accept only on strict 1e-12 improvement of the       │
│                          │ global max KVPR). This handles size-vs-rate asymmetries that pure moves provably cannot   │
│                          │ fix, and strictly-decreasing acceptance guarantees termination and correctness.           │
