│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a greedy seed with 4 ordering variants and a move-only local     │
│                          │ search that only targets the single worst GPU. The new program adds: (1) a swap operator  │
│                          │ (exchange a model on the worst GPU with a model on another GPU) which enables             │
│                          │ improvements when no single move fits in memory, and (2) after the worst-GPU phase        │
│                          │ stalls, a second phase targeting the runner-up GPU, both gated with 1e-12                 │
│                          │ strict-improvement thresholds. It also increases move iterations (40→80) and keeps the    │
│                          │ multi-seed restarts to escape bad greedy orders. These extensions generalize the proven   │
│                          │ move pattern and broaden the neighborhood so the max KVPR can drop further.               │
