│ patch_name               │ random_multistart_local_search                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of relying on only 4 fixed greedy orderings, this version uses a randomized       │
│                          │ multistart strategy: it runs the proven greedy construction from many different model     │
│                          │ orderings (the 4 deterministic ones plus randomized priority permutations), applies the   │
│                          │ same atomic best-op local search (moves, 1-for-1, 2-for-1, 2-for-2 swaps) to each, and    │
│                          │ keeps the best result. A final pair-swap polish phase scans all GPU pairs applying the    │
│                          │ best max-KVPR-reducing operation lexicographically (first lowering the max, then the      │
│                          │ second-highest). Randomization escapes the local optima that fixed orderings get stuck    │
│                          │ in, while the bounded local search keeps runtime negligible.                              │
